the first time I saw Sidhu it was in a  small shop in the old town of Dubai I  just fell in love with this patterns so  I thought that it would look really  stunning to take something so Bedouin  and so heritage and make it so modern  [Music]  my name is Katia kofta knowledge I live  in Dubai and I'm a fashion designer and  working with Sidhu is my big passion  Sidhu was originally made by Bedouin  women in the desert they would weave  them for weeks and months but there are  still amazing artisans that make it by  hand so it's a very very complicated art  and it's actually an art that is  disappearing when you touch this fabric  you really feel it's so different it has  a soul  I always just set myself free and I do  whatever I want with fabric a lot of  inspiration comes from traveling from  living in different countries living in  London observing different cultures and  finding something that exists in one  culture and translating it into another  culture the most interesting thing about  this fabric is the stripes that you can  take the same color the same fabric and  reconstruct it in so many ways one  stripe can go horizontally one stripe  can go vertically one strike and go  across so you create a very different  movement on the body working and  creating in Dubai it's a truly unique  experience everything is coming up the  pop art the music so it's just pure calm  inspiration nothing stops me I can go  and buy fabrics at 1:00 a.m. I can  finish my photoshoot at 3:00 a.m. you  feel like anything you desire you can  accomplish the why is the city where the  world impossible doesn't exist I think  my project was to do is something global  I love to see women wearing it and being  complimented and feeling special and I  only see very beautiful interesting  future  [Music]
 

